# Mutation plan for the group CRUD and membership family — `api4/group.go`'s seven writes and the
# `model.Group` / `model.GroupMember` validators they run behind the licence gate.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/group-writes.plan
#
# Two populations, and they are testing different things.
#
# The sixteen **model** mutations test `fixtures/behaviour_group.json` — the corpus generated by
# `reference/dump/behaviour_group.go`. Those validators were ported before this round and passed
# their new `go_parity` suite on the first run, which CLAUDE.md is explicit is not evidence. What
# is under test here is whether the corpus *discriminates*: the byte-vs-rune reading of the name
# cap, the order of every refusal chain, the `plugin_` prefix being a prefix and not a substring,
# the reserved-name branch's un-prefixed `where`, and the `||` in the remote-id condition that
# makes an over-long remote id illegal on a `custom` group that needs none.
#
# The six **router** mutations test the registrations themselves, which is the only new logic in
# the handlers: every one of the seven opens with `requireLicense` and answers the same 501, so a
# route registered on the wrong method or dropped entirely still produces a byte-identical body —
# from Go. Only `x-mmrs-served-by` can tell, which is why every parity assertion checks it.
#
# `charset-drops-empty-guard` is expected to SURVIVE and is here to record why: the `!name.is_empty()`
# in `is_valid_group_name_chars` mirrors the `+` in Go's `^[a-z0-9\.\-_]+$`, and the only caller
# rejects an empty name for its *length* first. The branch is unreachable through `is_valid_name`,
# so no fixture can reach it and the guard is defensive parity with the regex, not live logic.
#
# `scripts/mutations/groups.plan` is the sibling plan for the ten group **reads**, and its three
# `answer()` mutations already cover the body every one of these seven writes shares. Nothing here
# repeats them.
#
# The two controls are a binding rename and a reorder of two independent assignments in `Patch`.
# If either comes back CAUGHT the harness is deciding verdicts on something other than the
# mutation and the whole batch is void.

name-length-is-runes	crates/mm-model/src/group.rs	if name.is_empty() || name.len() > GROUP_NAME_MAX_LENGTH {	if name.is_empty() || name.chars().count() > GROUP_NAME_MAX_LENGTH {	unit	group::go_parity
name-length-off-by-one	crates/mm-model/src/group.rs	if name.is_empty() || name.len() > GROUP_NAME_MAX_LENGTH {	if name.is_empty() || name.len() >= GROUP_NAME_MAX_LENGTH {	unit	group::go_parity
